<figure id="S4.F4" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.10584v1/qualitative-7rows.png" id="S4.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:685/1196;" width="685" height="1196" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 4</span>: </span><span id="S4.F4.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
<span id="S4.F4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Qualitative results.</span> Marigold-SSD generally produces smoother depth maps than Marigold-DC <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">65</a>]</cite>, which tends to over-refine details that can lead to unrealistic scene structures.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S4.F5" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.10584v1/qualitative-kitti-2rows.png" id="S4.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:685/156;" width="685" height="156" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 5</span>: </span><span id="S4.F5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Qualitative results.<span id="S4.F5.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Both Marigold-SSD and Marigold-DC tend to underestimate sky depth on KITTI and DDAD, consistent with prior Marigold limitations and limited conditioning information in the sky, while they differ in how they estimate fine scene details.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
